## Legacy migration ledger (2026-10-28, code for owner review)

Owner authorizes simple uncovered feature cases plus a deferred/partial table. Static-only: no Nix, parser, formatter, evaluation, build, VM or legacy shell execution. Legacy scripts/fixtures and production behavior remain unchanged in this batch. Item3 stays pending.

Current tests/default.nix registers 35 explicit executable paths (30 newly authored module cases, one extended existing HM case, four other retained cases). Every entry uses ordinary callPackage and direct testers.runNixOSTest. It returns tests // { allTests = linkFarmFromDrvs "all-tests" (builtins.attrValues tests); }; no checker. Flake exports only checks.${defaultSystem}.tests = flake-inputs.self.packages.${defaultSystem}.projectTests.allTests. Link names use each derivation's name; all 35 declared test names are distinct by static source review. symlinkJoin would merge directory contents and takes an attribute set, so it is not used.

Every one of the 134 exported legacy assertion/expected-error keys is listed below. Status describes SOURCE COVERAGE, never passing execution: authored = concrete replacement scenario; partial = named remainder explicitly remains; deferred = non-simple/intrinsic prerequisite unresolved; excluded = owner rejected inventories/upstream/broad-policy comparisons. Data witnesses may differ as recorded. No equivalence, runtime, aggregate memory or success proof is inferred.

