## Current code orientation

Paths below are repository-relative. Re-read their live revisions when designing
system details; these observations are support, not additional contracts.

- `flake.nix` assembles `config/nixos.nix`, `modules/nixos.nix`, package support,
  external modules and overlays, and supplies project `lib`, `flake-inputs` and
  `pkgsUnstable` to assembled systems. The reusable test environment needs its
  own deliberate boundary rather than importing that whole host assembly.
- `lib/system.nix` owns `extend`, production/validation configuration assembly
  and host package exports. Automatic `extend` inheritance remains deferred.
- `modules/home/homedir.nix` and canonical 001 specify `home.enable` and `hm`:
  raw deferred declarations are applied only when active; reads project the
  final merged Home Manager user when active. The primary login separately
  selects OS-account creation. Those are completed inputs to runner design.
- Canonical 001 also specifies disabled-by-default optional modules; the archived
  `conditional-module-activation` change implemented that preparation.
- `config/hardware/bootable/default.nix` is now in the policy layer. The old
  claim that reusable bootable modules require nixos-generators support must be
  re-evaluated before choosing external modules for tests.
- `lib/modules.nix` owns the by-name overlay helper and `pkgsOrigin`;
  `pkgs/default.nix` adds that overlay and publishes `pkgsUnstable`.
- Both current callers use `testers.runNixOSTest`: `tests/pkgs/specd.nix` and
  `tests/pkgs/specd-bootstrap.nix`. Include both when planning compatibility
  evidence. No project-aware wrapper is present in inspected current sources.

## Retained direction and open system decisions

- Preserve project capability availability, focused minimal nodes and existing
  package/test compatibility as requirement-level needs.
- Retain the existing runner: the user rejected the separate-runner fallback
  after the final-review finding. The accepted proposal permits that fallback,
  but it is no longer a live candidate. The user's current correction
  requires automatic availability of `modules/nixos.nix` and its shared support
  in test VM nodes, with activation through each node's existing capability
  configuration. The legacy `projectModules.enable` switch was rejected; it is
  no longer a design candidate. Prior optional-module work enables this model.
- Reuse project capability definitions. Exclude automatic policy from `config/`,
  concrete hosts and private-value validation stubs. Tests supply intrinsic
  inputs for selected functionality.
- Determine necessary external support modules from the current reusable module
  collection. Do not inherit the old Home Manager/nixos-generators shortlist
  without checking actual consumers and disabled-feature behavior.
- Guest package-set construction, overlays, evaluation arguments, guest platform
  selection and composition with upstream extension interfaces require system
  design. Check upstream runner sources from the locked input at that time.
- Preserve existing 003 REQ-001 validation-configuration/private-stub contracts.
  Add focused validation checks without expanding unrelated testing scope.
- Historical `/workspace/.setup` probes, derivation counts and missing-KVM/PRoot
  limitations are evidence from a former environment. Fresh technical checks
  are needed before drawing current evaluation, build or runtime conclusions.

