- Accepted system extends existing `testers.runNixOSTest`. The support module
  always supplies reusable/HM definitions and project arguments. It preserves
  the final upstream `node.pkgsReadOnly`, including its default. Only `pkgs/`
  and the overlay contributions in `modules/hardware/hosts/` and
  `modules/hardware/development/programmers/stm32/` are gated in read-only mode.
  Production guards belong on those overlay definitions, not on capability
  definitions or a test-maintained copy/blacklist of project modules.
- Frozen mode preserves the supplied package set, including role flags and
  variants; it cannot regenerate guest-specific variants or publish missing
  packages. Mutable mode follows upstream package selection and applies project
  and caller overlays. The previous `nixpkgs.pkgs = mkDefault node.pkgs` rule
  was removed: upstream ignores test-level `node.pkgs` when mutable, so that
  rule changed its semantics. Project argument defaults survive `extendNixOS`.
